From c92246005dbbb51e41223ffba982309a46f2964e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hbadi <badi.hamid@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 10:26:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Declare logs::error as noreturn

It throws unconditionally, so it never comes back, but nothing said so and the
compiler could not know. The one place it shows is sl::allpartition without the
Gmsh API, whose whole body is a message and that call: gcc reports "control
reaches end of non-void function", clang "non-void function does not return a
value in all control paths". Both are right about what they can see.

The attribute is the honest fix rather than a return value invented to quiet the
warning, which would have added dead code and said nothing. It also documents
the contract at every other call site, and lets the compiler drop the code that
would follow.

Declared in the header, so every translation unit agrees; logs.cpp includes it,
and the definition already never returns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/logs.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/logs.h b/src/logs.h
index 707f15c4..efe84eac 100755
--- a/src/logs.h
+++ b/src/logs.h
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ class logs
 
         std::ostream& msg(void);
         
-        void error(void);
+        [[noreturn]] void error(void);
     
 };
 
